IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-ch1-preliminary`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 15: Aids to interpretation.
--
-- The rules about periods of time (ss 149, 151, 151A, 151C (6)) and about the application date (s 146 (4)) are in `act-interpretation-time.l4`.
-- This module holds the rest of chapter 15: the commonly used terms (s 144), gender and number (s 145), may and must (s 146),
-- changes of drafting practice (s 147), terms in instruments (s 148), distance (s 150), things for which no time is fixed (s 151B),
-- the power to extend time (s 151C), continuing obligations (s 152), definitions (ss 155 to 157),
-- references to people and things (ss 160 to 169B) and preserved privileges (ss 170 and 171).
-- The definitions that sit inside these sections are in `act-section-definitions.l4`.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 15, Aids to interpretation`

§§ `Part 15.1: General`

-- src:1846 | A definition in the dictionary, part 1 applies to all Acts and statutory instruments.
@ref s 144 (src:1846-1846)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing this Act might be applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144: a definition in the dictionary, part 1 applies to the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act (including this Act)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF
    `singular`
    `plural`

-- src:1850 | In an Act or statutory instrument—
-- src:1851 | (a) words indicating a gender include every other gender; and
@ref s 145 (a) (src:1850-1851)
GIVEN theWordIndicatesAGender IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145 (a): the word includes every other gender` MEANS
    IF   theWordIndicatesAGender
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1852 | (b) words in the singular number include the plural and words in the plural number include the singular.
@ref s 145 (b) (src:1852-1852)
GIVEN number IS A `Number of a word`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Number of a word`
`s 145 (b): the numbers the word covers` MEANS LIST `singular`, `plural`

DECLARE `Word used in relation to a function` IS ONE OF
    `may, or a similar term`
    `must, or a similar term`
    `another word`

DECLARE `What the word indicates about the function` IS ONE OF
    `the function may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion`
    `the function is required to be exercised`

-- src:1855 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, the word may, or a similar term, used in relation to a function indicates that the function may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion.
-- src:1856 | Note Function is defined in the dictionary, pt 1 to include authority, duty and power.
-- src:1857 | (2) In an Act or statutory instrument, the word must, or a similar term, used in relation to a function indicates that the function is required to be exercised.
@ref s 146 (1), (2) (src:1855-1857)
GIVEN word IS A `Word used in relation to a function`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the word indicates about the function`
`s 146 (1), (2): what the word indicates about the function` MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `may, or a similar term` THEN JUST `the function may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion`
    WHEN `must, or a similar term` THEN JUST `the function is required to be exercised`
    WHEN `another word` THEN NOTHING

-- s 147 (3), (4), (5): ideas in two provisions of an older form and a newer form are not regarded as different only because of the words or the structure.
-- src:1872 | (3) If an Act or statutory instrument is amended so that it contains an older form of legislative expression in a provision and a newer form in another, the ideas in the 2 provisions must not be regarded as different only because different words are used or the provisions are structured in different ways.
-- src:1873 | (4) Subsection (3) also applies if the provisions are in different Acts or statutory instruments.
-- src:1874 | (5) Also, if an Act or statutory instrument is amended so that a provision containing an older form of legislative expression is replaced (whether or not in the same position) by a provision in a newer form, the ideas in the 2 provisions must not be regarded as different only because different words are used or the provisions are structured in different ways.
@ref s 147 (3) to (5) (src:1872-1874)
GIVEN theOnlyDifferenceIsTheWordsUsedOrTheStructure IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147 (3) to (5): the ideas in the two provisions are regarded as different` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyDifferenceIsTheWordsUsedOrTheStructure
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1875 | (6) In deciding whether the ideas are different, regard must be had to the context and history of the 2 provisions.
@ref s 147 (6) (src:1875-1875)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 147 (6): regard must be had to the context and history of the 2 provisions` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1876 | (7) Subsection (6) does not limit the matters to which regard may be had.
@ref s 147 (7) (src:1876-1876)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 147 (7): subsection (6) limits the matters to which regard may be had` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1881 | Terms used in a statutory instrument have the same meanings as they have, from time to time, in the Act or statutory instrument (the authorising law), or the relevant provisions of the authorising law, under which the instrument is made or in force.
@ref s 148 (src:1881-1881)
GIVEN meaningInTheAuthorisingLawFromTimeToTime IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 148: the meaning of a term used in a statutory instrument` MEANS meaningInTheAuthorisingLawFromTimeToTime

-- src:1887 | In applying an Act or statutory instrument, distance is to be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 150 (src:1887-1887)
GIVEN measuredInAStraightLineOnAHorizontalPlane IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150: the distance is measured as the Act requires` MEANS measuredInAStraightLineOnAHorizontalPlane

-- src:1890 | (1) This section applies in working out periods of 1 day or longer for an Act or statutory instrument, whether the period is a period in the future or the past.
@ref s 151 (1) (src:1890-1890)
GIVEN thePeriodIsOfOneDayOrLonger IS A BOOLEAN, theWorkingOutIsForAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151 (1): s 151 applies in working out the period` MEANS thePeriodIsOfOneDayOrLonger AND theWorkingOutIsForAnActOrStatutoryInstrument

DECLARE `When a thing with no fixed time must or may be done` IS ONE OF
    `as soon as possible and as often as needed`

-- src:1955 | (1) This section applies if—
-- src:1956 | (a) under an Act or statutory instrument, something must or may be done; but
-- src:1957 | (b) no time is provided for doing the thing.
@ref s 151B (1) (src:1955-1957)
GIVEN somethingMustOrMayBeDoneUnderAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, noTimeIsProvidedForDoingTheThing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151B (1): s 151B applies to the thing` MEANS somethingMustOrMayBeDoneUnderAnActOrStatutoryInstrument AND noTimeIsProvidedForDoingTheThing

-- src:1958 | (2) The thing must or may be done as soon as possible and as often as needed.
@ref s 151B (2) (src:1958-1958)
GIVEN s151BApplies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `When a thing with no fixed time must or may be done`
`s 151B (2): when the thing must or may be done` MEANS
    IF   s151BApplies
    THEN JUST `as soon as possible and as often as needed`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1961 | (1) This section applies if, under an Act or statutory instrument—
-- src:1962 | (a) something must or may be done on a particular day or within a particular period of time; but
-- src:1963 | (b) a court or other entity has power to extend the time (the relevant time) for doing the thing.
@ref s 151C (1) (src:1961-1963)
GIVEN somethingMustOrMayBeDoneOnADayOrWithinAPeriod IS A BOOLEAN, aCourtOrOtherEntityHasPowerToExtendTheTime IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151C (1): s 151C applies to the thing` MEANS somethingMustOrMayBeDoneOnADayOrWithinAPeriod AND aCourtOrOtherEntityHasPowerToExtendTheTime

-- src:1964 | (2) A person may apply to the court or other entity for the relevant time to be extended even though the relevant time has ended.
@ref s 151C (2) (src:1964-1964)
GIVEN s151CApplies IS A BOOLEAN, theRelevantTimeHasEnded IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 151C (2): a person may apply for the relevant time to be extended` MEANS
    IF   s151CApplies
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1965 | (3) The court or other entity may extend the relevant time even though the relevant time has ended.
@ref s 151C (3) (src:1965-1965)
GIVEN s151CApplies IS A BOOLEAN, theRelevantTimeHasEnded IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 151C (3): the court or other entity may extend the relevant time` MEANS
    IF   s151CApplies
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1968 | (5) This section applies only to an applicable law or applicable provision.
@ref s 151C (5) (src:1968-1968)
GIVEN dayTheLawWasEnactedOrMade IS A DATE, dayAProvisionWasInserted IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 151C (5): s 151C applies to the law or provision` MEANS
    `s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` dayTheLawWasEnactedOrMade dayAProvisionWasInserted

-- src:1975 | If, under a provision of an Act or statutory instrument, an act is required to be done, the obligation to do the act continues until the act is done even if—
-- src:1976 | (a) the provision required the act to be done within a particular period or before a particular time, and the period has ended or the time has passed; or
-- src:1977 | (b) someone has been convicted of an offence in relation to failure to do the act.
@ref s 152 (src:1975-1977)
GIVEN theActIsRequiredByAProvision IS A BOOLEAN, theActHasBeenDone IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152: the obligation to do the act continues` MEANS
    IF   theActIsRequiredByAProvision
    THEN JUST (NOT theActHasBeenDone)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 15.2: Definitions`

-- src:1983 | (1) A definition in an Act or statutory instrument applies except so far as the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 155 (1) (src:1983-1983)
GIVEN theContraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 155 (1): the definition applies` MEANS (NOT theContraryIntentionAppears)

DECLARE `Where a definition is placed` IS ONE OF
    `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument`
    `in a section of the Act or instrument`

DECLARE `What the Act or instrument provides about where the definition applies` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `a more limited application`
    `a broader application`

DECLARE `How far a definition applies` IS ONE OF
    `the entire Act or instrument`
    `only the section it is in`
    `the more limited part the Act or instrument provides for`
    `the broader part the Act or instrument provides for`

-- src:1988 | (1) A definition in the dictionary to an Act or statutory instrument applies to the entire Act or instrument unless the Act or instrument provides for the definition to have a more limited application.
-- src:1989 | Examples
-- src:1990 | 1 The dictionary to the ABC Act 1999 includes the signpost definition ‘x—see the XYZ Act 1998, section 3.’. There is nothing in the ABC Act 1999 indicating the intended application of the definition of x. The definition of x in the XYZ Act 1998, s 3, therefore, applies to the entire ABC Act 1999.
-- src:1991 | 2 In an Act, the word z is defined in the dictionary. The definition provides, in part, that ‘z, in part 4 (Registration of vehicles), means ...’. The definition of z applies only to pt 4.
-- src:1992 | 3 In pt 6 of an Act (which is headed ‘Part 6 Complaints’), the word a is defined in s 50. The section is not divided into subsections but contains a number of definitions. Section 50 begins with the words ‘In this part:’. However, the dictionary to the Act contains the following definition:
-- src:1993 | a—see section 50.
-- src:1994 | The definition of a applies to the entire Act (compare s (2) example 2).
-- src:1995 | Note 1 See s 144 (Meaning of commonly-used terms) for the application of the definitions in this Act, dict, pt 1.
-- src:1996 | Note 2 Section 148 (Terms used in instruments have same meanings as in authorising laws) provides that terms used in a statutory instrument have the same meaning as they have in the Act or statutory instrument under which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:1997 | (2) A definition in a section of an Act or statutory instrument applies only to the section unless the Act or instrument provides for the definition to have a broader application.
-- src:1998 | Examples
-- src:1999 | 1 This Act, s 255 (7) (Forms) contains definitions of form 1 and form 2 as tagged terms. There is nothing in this Act indicating that the definitions apply outside s 255. The definitions apply only to s 255.
-- src:2000 | 2 In pt 6 of an Act (which is headed ‘Part 6 Complaints’), the word a is defined in s 50. The section is not divided into subsections but contains a number of definitions. Section 50 begins with the words ‘In this part:’. However, the dictionary to the Act contains the following definition:
-- src:2001 | a, for part 6 (Complaints)—see section 50.
-- src:2002 | The definition of a applies to all of pt 6, but not to provisions of the Act outside pt 6 (compare s (1) example 3).
-- src:2003 | 3 In an Act, the word b is defined in a section, which is not divided into subsections but contains a number of definitions. The section begins with the words ‘In this Act:’. The definition of b applies to the entire Act.
-- src:2004 | (3) A definition in a section of an Act or statutory instrument applies to the entire section unless the Act or instrument provides for the definition to have a more limited application.
@ref s 156 (1) to (3) (src:1988-2004)
GIVEN placed IS A `Where a definition is placed`, provided IS A `What the Act or instrument provides about where the definition applies`
GIVETH A MAYBE `How far a definition applies`
`s 156 (1) to (3): how far the definition applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER placed
    WHEN `in the dictionary to the Act or instrument` THEN
        CONSIDER provided
        WHEN `nothing` THEN JUST `the entire Act or instrument`
        WHEN `a more limited application` THEN JUST `the more limited part the Act or instrument provides for`
        WHEN `a broader application` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `in a section of the Act or instrument` THEN
        CONSIDER provided
        WHEN `nothing` THEN JUST `only the section it is in`
        WHEN `a more limited application` THEN JUST `the more limited part the Act or instrument provides for`
        WHEN `a broader application` THEN JUST `the broader part the Act or instrument provides for`

DECLARE `What a reference to a section is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `a section`
    `the corresponding provision`

-- src:2007 | (4) In applying this section to an Act or statutory instrument that is divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section is a reference to a corresponding provision of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 156 (4) (src:2007-2007)
GIVEN theActIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a reference to a section is a reference to`
`s 156 (4): what a reference to a section is a reference to` MEANS
    IF   theActIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections
    THEN `the corresponding provision`
    ELSE `a section`

-- src:2011 | If an Act or statutory instrument defines a term, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the term have corresponding meanings.
@ref s 157 (src:2011-2011)
GIVEN theActOrInstrumentDefinesTheTerm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 157: the other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the term have corresponding meanings` MEANS theActOrInstrumentDefinesTheTerm

§§ `Part 15.3: References to various entities and things`

DECLARE `Kind of party` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a corporation`
    `another kind of party`

-- src:2019 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to a person generally includes a reference to a corporation as well as an individual.
@ref s 160 (1) (src:2019-2019)
GIVEN party IS A `Kind of party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160 (1): a reference to a person generally includes the party` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of party` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2020 | (2) Subsection (1) is not displaced only because there is an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act or statutory instrument.
@ref s 160 (2) (src:2020-2020)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsAnExpressReferenceToEitherAnIndividualOrACorporationElsewhere IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160 (2): subsection (1) is displaced` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsAnExpressReferenceToEitherAnIndividualOrACorporationElsewhere
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What an expression refers to` IS ONE OF
    `a person generally`
    `a corporation`
    `an individual`

-- src:2021 | Examples—references to a person generally
-- src:2022 | 1 another person
-- src:2023 | 2 anyone else
-- src:2024 | 3 party
-- src:2025 | 4 someone else
-- src:2026 | 5 employer
-- src:2027 | Examples—express references to a corporation
-- src:2028 | 1 body corporate
-- src:2029 | 2 company
-- src:2030 | Examples—express references to an individual
-- src:2031 | 1 adult
-- src:2032 | 2 child
-- src:2033 | 3 spouse
-- src:2034 | 4 driver
@ref s 160, examples (references to a person generally, to a corporation, to an individual) (src:2021-2034)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `What an expression refers to`
`s 160, examples: what the expression refers to` MEANS
    IF   elem expression (LIST "another person", "anyone else", "party", "someone else", "employer")
    THEN JUST `a person generally`
    ELSE IF   elem expression (LIST "body corporate", "company")
         THEN JUST `a corporation`
         ELSE IF   elem expression (LIST "adult", "child", "spouse", "driver")
              THEN JUST `an individual`
              ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2035 | (3) Subsection (2) does not limit the operation of section 6.
@ref s 160 (3) (src:2035-2035)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 160 (3): subsection (2) limits the operation of section 6` MEANS FALSE

-- src:2039 | (1) A provision of a law that creates an offence (whether indictable or summary) applies to corporations as well as to individuals.
-- src:2040 | (2) A provision of a law that creates an offence can apply to a corporation even though contravention of the provision is punishable by imprisonment (with or without another penalty).
@ref s 161 (1), (2) (src:2039-2040)
GIVEN party IS A `Kind of party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161 (1), (2): a provision of a law that creates an offence applies to the party` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of party` THEN NOTHING

-- s 161 (3): the period of imprisonment is given in months so that "1 year" is 12 and "2 years" is 24.
-- src:2045 | (3) If a corporation is convicted of an offence and, apart from this subsection, the penalty for the offence is a period of imprisonment only, the court may impose a maximum penalty of—
-- src:2046 | (a) if the period of imprisonment is not longer than 6 months—50 penalty units; and
-- src:2047 | (b) if the period of imprisonment is longer than 6 months but not longer than 1 year—100 penalty units; and
-- src:2048 | (c) if the period of imprisonment is longer than 1 year but not longer than 2 years—200 penalty units; and
-- src:2049 | (d) if the period of imprisonment is longer than 2 years but not longer than 5 years—500 penalty units; and
-- src:2050 | (e) if the period of imprisonment is longer than 5 years but not longer than 10 years—1 000 penalty units; and
-- src:2051 | (f) if the period of imprisonment is longer than 10 years—1 500 penalty units.
@ref s 161 (3) (src:2045-2051)
GIVEN theCorporationIsConvicted IS A BOOLEAN, thePenaltyIsAPeriodOfImprisonmentOnly IS A BOOLEAN, monthsOfImprisonment IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` MEANS
    IF   NOT (theCorporationIsConvicted AND thePenaltyIsAPeriodOfImprisonmentOnly AND monthsOfImprisonment GREATER THAN 0)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   monthsOfImprisonment AT MOST 6
         THEN JUST 50
         ELSE IF   monthsOfImprisonment AT MOST 12
              THEN JUST 100
              ELSE IF   monthsOfImprisonment AT MOST 24
                   THEN JUST 200
                   ELSE IF   monthsOfImprisonment AT MOST 60
                        THEN JUST 500
                        ELSE IF   monthsOfImprisonment AT MOST 120
                             THEN JUST 1000
                             ELSE JUST 1500

-- src:2053 | (4) In this section:
-- src:2054 | law means an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument.
@ref s 161 (4), definition of law (src:2053-2054)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 161 (4): the kind of document is a law for this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- ss 162 and 163: who a reference to "the Minister" or "the director-general" is a reference to.
-- The Ministers (or administrative units) are given by name so that the answer can say which of them the reference is to.
DECLARE `Who administers or is responsible for a provision` HAS
    `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `Who a reference is to` HAS
    `those the reference is to` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `any one of them` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2059 | (2) In a provision of an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to the Minister without identifying the Minister’s title or portfolio is a reference to—
-- src:2060 | (a) the Minister for the time being administering the provision; or
-- src:2061 | (b) if, for the time being, different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters—
-- src:2062 | (i) if only 1 Minister administers the provision in relation to the relevant matter—the Minister; or
-- src:2063 | (ii) if 2 or more Ministers administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter—any of the Ministers; or
-- src:2064 | (c) if paragraph (b) does not apply and, for the time being, 2 or more Ministers administer the provision—any of the Ministers.
@ref s 162 (2) (src:2059-2064)
GIVEN f IS A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who a reference is to`
`s 162 (2): who a reference to the Minister without a title is a reference to` MEANS `who the reference is to, given who administers or is responsible` f

-- src:2072 | (2) In a provision of an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to the director-general without identifying the director-general’s title is a reference to—
-- src:2073 | (a) the director-general of the administrative unit responsible for the provision; or
-- src:2074 | (b) if, for the time being, different administrative units are responsible for the provision in relation to different matters—
-- src:2075 | (i) if only 1 administrative unit is responsible for the provision in relation to the relevant matter—the director-general of the administrative unit; or
-- src:2076 | (ii) if 2 or more administrative units are responsible for the provision in relation to the relevant matter—the director-general of any of the administrative units; or
-- src:2077 | (c) if paragraph (b) does not apply and, for the time being, 2 or more administrative units are responsible for the provision—the director-general of any of the administrative units.
@ref s 163 (2) (src:2072-2077)
GIVEN f IS A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who a reference is to`
`s 163 (2): which administrative unit's director-general a reference to the director-general without a title is a reference to` MEANS `who the reference is to, given who administers or is responsible` f

-- The shape of the rule in s 162 (2) (a) to (c) and s 163 (2) (a) to (c) is the same:
-- (b) where different ones administer or are responsible for different matters, the one for the relevant matter, or any of them if there are two or more;
-- (c) where (b) does not apply and two or more administer or are responsible, any of them; (a) otherwise, the one that does.
GIVEN f IS A `Who administers or is responsible for a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who a reference is to`
`who the reference is to, given who administers or is responsible` MEANS
    IF   f's `different ones administer or are responsible in relation to different matters`
    THEN `the one or any of` (f's `those who administer or are responsible in relation to the relevant matter`)
    ELSE `the one or any of` (f's `all of those who for the time being administer or are responsible for the provision`)

GIVEN names IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who a reference is to`
`the one or any of` MEANS
    CONSIDER names
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER rest
        WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS names, `any one of them` IS FALSE)
        WHEN second FOLLOWED BY others THEN JUST (`Who a reference is to` WITH `those the reference is to` IS names, `any one of them` IS TRUE)

-- src:2057 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to a Minister is a reference to the Chief Minister or a Minister appointed under the Self-Government Act, section 41.
@ref s 162 (1) (src:2057-2057)
GIVEN isTheChiefMinister IS A BOOLEAN, isAMinisterAppointedUnderTheSelfGovernmentActSection41 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162 (1): the person is a Minister` MEANS isTheChiefMinister OR isAMinisterAppointedUnderTheSelfGovernmentActSection41

-- src:2065 | (3) In subsection (2):
-- src:2066 | Minister includes a Minister for the time being acting on behalf of the Minister or 2 or more Ministers.
@ref s 162 (3) (src:2065-2066)
GIVEN isAMinisterForTheTimeBeingActingOnBehalfOfTheMinisterOrOfTwoOrMoreMinisters IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162 (3): the reference to the Minister in subsection (2) includes the person` MEANS
    IF   isAMinisterForTheTimeBeingActingOnBehalfOfTheMinisterOrOfTwoOrMoreMinisters
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2067 | (4) If an Act or statutory instrument mentions a Minister and identifies the Minister by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a stated Act, statutory instrument or provision, subsection (2) applies as if references in paragraphs (a) to (c) to the provision were references to the stated Act, instrument or provision.
@ref s 162 (4) (src:2067-2067)
GIVEN theProvision IS A STRING, theStatedActInstrumentOrProvision IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 162 (4): the provision whose administration decides which Minister the reference is to` MEANS `the stated one if there is one, otherwise the provision` theProvision theStatedActInstrumentOrProvision

-- src:2079 | (3) If an Act or statutory instrument mentions a director-general and identifies the director-general by reference to the fact that the director-general is the director-general of the administrative unit responsible for a stated Act, statutory instrument or provision, subsection (2) applies as if references in paragraphs (a) to (c) to the provision were references to the stated Act, instrument or provision.
@ref s 163 (3) (src:2079-2079)
GIVEN theProvision IS A STRING, theStatedActInstrumentOrProvision IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 163 (3): the provision whose responsibility decides which director-general the reference is to` MEANS `the stated one if there is one, otherwise the provision` theProvision theStatedActInstrumentOrProvision

GIVEN theProvision IS A STRING, theStatedActInstrumentOrProvision IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the stated one if there is one, otherwise the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER theStatedActInstrumentOrProvision
    WHEN JUST stated THEN stated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN theProvision

-- src:2071 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to a director-general is a reference to a person employed under the Public Sector Management Act, section 31 (Engagement of SES member) to perform the duties of an office of director-general.
@ref s 163 (1) (src:2071-2071)
GIVEN isEmployedUnderThePublicSectorManagementActSection31ToPerformTheDutiesOfAnOfficeOfDirectorGeneral IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 163 (1): the person is a director-general` MEANS isEmployedUnderThePublicSectorManagementActSection31ToPerformTheDutiesOfAnOfficeOfDirectorGeneral

DECLARE `Publisher of a standard` IS ONE OF
    `Standards Australia`
    `Standards Australia and Standards New Zealand, jointly`

-- src:2086 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference consisting of the words ‘Australian Standard’ or ‘AS’ followed by a number is a reference to the standard so numbered published by or on behalf of Standards Australia.
-- src:2087 | (2) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference consisting of the words ‘Australian/New Zealand Standard’ or ‘AS/NZS’ followed by a number is a reference to the standard so numbered published jointly by or on behalf of Standards Australia and Standards New Zealand.
@ref s 164 (1), (2) (src:2086-2087)
GIVEN wordsBeforeTheNumber IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Publisher of a standard`
`s 164 (1), (2): the publisher of the standard a reference names` MEANS
    IF   elem wordsBeforeTheNumber (LIST "Australian Standard", "AS")
    THEN JUST `Standards Australia`
    ELSE IF   elem wordsBeforeTheNumber (LIST "Australian/New Zealand Standard", "AS/NZS")
         THEN JUST `Standards Australia and Standards New Zealand, jointly`
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2090 | In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference (whether by name or description) to a committee of the Legislative Assembly that no longer exists is a reference to the committee of the Assembly nominated by the Speaker either generally or for the provision containing the reference.
@ref s 165 (src:2090-2090)
GIVEN theCommitteeNoLongerExists IS A BOOLEAN, theCommitteeNominatedBySpeakerGenerallyOrForTheProvision IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 165: the committee a reference to a committee that no longer exists is a reference to` MEANS
    IF   theCommitteeNoLongerExists
    THEN theCommitteeNominatedBySpeakerGenerallyOrForTheProvision
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of person with an interest` IS ONE OF
    `the person with the interest`
    `the person's personal representative`
    `the person's successor`
    `the person's assign`
    `someone else`

-- src:2093 | In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes a reference to the person’s personal representatives, successors and assigns.
@ref s 168 (src:2093-2093)
GIVEN who IS A `Kind of person with an interest`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168: a reference to a person with an interest in land or other property includes the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `the person with the interest` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the person's personal representative` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the person's successor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the person's assign` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2094 | Examples—references to people with interests in land
-- src:2095 | 1 proprietor
-- src:2096 | 2 transferor or transferee
-- src:2097 | 3 mortgagor or mortgagee
-- src:2098 | 4 lessor or lessee
-- src:2099 | 5 sublessor or sublessee
-- src:2100 | 6 trustee
@ref s 168, examples (references to people with interests in land) (src:2094-2100)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 168, examples: the expression is a reference to a person with an interest in land` MEANS
    IF   elem expression (LIST "proprietor", "transferor or transferee", "mortgagor or mortgagee", "lessor or lessee", "sublessor or sublessee", "trustee")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Relationship to a person` IS ONE OF
    `someone who lives with the person in a domestic partnership`
    `a spouse of the person`
    `a civil union partner of the person`
    `a civil partner of the person`
    `someone else`

-- src:2103 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to a person’s domestic partner is a reference to someone who lives with the person in a domestic partnership, and includes a reference to a spouse, civil union partner or civil partner of the person.
@ref s 169 (1) (src:2103-2103)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship to a person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169 (1): a reference to a person's domestic partner includes the relationship` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `someone who lives with the person in a domestic partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a spouse of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a civil union partner of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a civil partner of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2104 | (2) In an Act or statutory instrument, a domestic partnership is the relationship between 2 people living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis.
@ref s 169 (2) (src:2104-2104)
GIVEN twoPeopleAreLivingTogetherAsACouple IS A BOOLEAN, onAGenuineDomesticBasis IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 169 (2): the relationship between the two people is a domestic partnership` MEANS twoPeopleAreLivingTogetherAsACouple AND onAGenuineDomesticBasis

-- s 169 (2) Example: the indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership (copied from the text, one string per line).
-- src:2105 | Example—indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership
-- src:2106 | 1 the length of their relationship
-- src:2107 | 2 whether they are living together
-- src:2108 | 3 if they are living together—how long and under what circumstances they have lived together
-- src:2109 | 4 whether there is a sexual relationship between them
-- src:2110 | 5 their degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between or by them
-- src:2111 | 6 the ownership, use and acquisition of their property, including any property that they own individually
-- src:2112 | 7 their degree of mutual commitment to a shared life
-- src:2113 | 8 whether they mutually care for and support children
-- src:2114 | 9 the performance of household duties
-- src:2115 | 10 the reputation, and public aspects, of the relationship between them
@ref s 169 (2), example (indicators) (src:2105-2115)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 169 (2), example: the indicators to decide whether 2 people are in a domestic partnership` MEANS
    LIST
        "the length of their relationship"
        , "whether they are living together"
        , "if they are living together—how long and under what circumstances they have lived together"
        , "whether there is a sexual relationship between them"
        , "their degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between or by them"
        , "the ownership, use and acquisition of their property, including any property that they own individually"
        , "their degree of mutual commitment to a shared life"
        , "whether they mutually care for and support children"
        , "the performance of household duties"
        , "the reputation, and public aspects, of the relationship between them"

DECLARE `Kind of relationship` IS ONE OF
    `a marriage`
    `a civil union`
    `a civil partnership`
    `another relationship`

-- src:2116 | (3) In an Act or statutory instrument, a reference to a domestic partnership includes a reference to a marriage, a civil union and a civil partnership.
@ref s 169 (3) (src:2116-2116)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Kind of relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169 (3): a reference to a domestic partnership includes the relationship` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `a marriage` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a civil union` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a civil partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another relationship` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2119 | (1) A transgender person is a person who—
-- src:2120 | (a) identifies as a member of a different sex by living, or seeking to live, as a member of that sex; or
-- src:2121 | (b) has identified as a member of a different sex by living as a member of that sex;
-- src:2122 | whether or not the person is a recognised transgender person.
@ref s 169A (1) (src:2119-2122)
GIVEN identifiesAsAMemberOfADifferentSexByLivingOrSeekingToLiveAsAMemberOfThatSex IS A BOOLEAN, hasIdentifiedAsAMemberOfADifferentSexByLivingAsAMemberOfThatSex IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 169A (1): the person is a transgender person` MEANS
    identifiesAsAMemberOfADifferentSexByLivingOrSeekingToLiveAsAMemberOfThatSex OR hasIdentifiedAsAMemberOfADifferentSexByLivingAsAMemberOfThatSex

-- src:2123 | (2) A transgender person includes a person who is thought of as a transgender person, whether or not the person is a recognised transgender person.
@ref s 169A (2) (src:2123-2123)
GIVEN isThoughtOfAsATransgenderPerson IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 169A (2): a transgender person includes the person` MEANS
    IF   isThoughtOfAsATransgenderPerson
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2124 | (3) A recognised transgender person is a person the record of whose sex is altered under the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1997, part 4 or the corresponding provisions of a law of a State or another Territory.
@ref s 169A (3) (src:2124-2124)
GIVEN theRecordOfTheirSexIsAlteredUnderTheBirthsDeathsAndMarriagesRegistrationAct1997Part4OrACorrespondingLawOfAStateOrAnotherTerritory IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 169A (3): the person is a recognised transgender person` MEANS theRecordOfTheirSexIsAlteredUnderTheBirthsDeathsAndMarriagesRegistrationAct1997Part4OrACorrespondingLawOfAStateOrAnotherTerritory

-- src:2127 | An intersex person is a person who has physical, hormonal or genetic features that are—
-- src:2128 | (a) not fully female or fully male; or
-- src:2129 | (b) a combination of male or female; or
-- src:2130 | (c) not female or male.
@ref s 169B (src:2127-2130)
GIVEN hasPhysicalHormonalOrGeneticFeatures IS A BOOLEAN, notFullyFemaleOrFullyMale IS A BOOLEAN, aCombinationOfMaleOrFemale IS A BOOLEAN, notFemaleOrMale IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 169B: the person is an intersex person` MEANS
    hasPhysicalHormonalOrGeneticFeatures AND (notFullyFemaleOrFullyMale OR aCombinationOfMaleOrFemale OR notFemaleOrMale)

§§ `Part 15.4: Preservation of certain common law privileges`

-- src:2135 | (1) An Act or statutory instrument must be interpreted to preserve the common law privileges against self-incrimination and exposure to the imposition of a civil penalty.
@ref s 170 (1) (src:2135-2135)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing this Act might be applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privileges against self-incrimination and exposure to the imposition of a civil penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act (including this Act)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2136 | (2) However, this section does not affect the operation of the Evidence Act 2011.
@ref s 170 (2) (src:2136-2136)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 170 (2): this section affects the operation of the Evidence Act 2011` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:2142 | (1) An Act or statutory instrument must be interpreted to preserve the common law privilege in relation to client legal privilege (also known as legal professional privilege).
@ref s 171 (1) (src:2142-2142)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing this Act might be applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171 (1): the thing must be interpreted to preserve the common law privilege in relation to client legal privilege` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act (including this Act)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2143 | (2) However, this section does not affect the operation of the Evidence Act 2011.
@ref s 171 (2) (src:2143-2143)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171 (2): this section affects the operation of the Evidence Act 2011` MEANS JUST FALSE
